
In this archive, I've included a set of data files with AUSTRALIAN
content.

Now, you have three choices as to what to use:

Firstly, use the supplied .dat files and you get American names/places.

Secondly, you could move the American.dat files out of the directory (or
rename them), and rename FILE.dat.aus to FILE.dat and use the Australian
data files.

Thirdly - best idea - is to setup TWO door directories, and use the
American Data files in one directory, and the Australian data files
in the other directory, thus giving you TWO doors!!

Note that the door looks for files of the form FILE.dat, so if you do
ever want to get it to read the Australian data files, they WILL have to
be renamed to FILE.dat

[PFD 23 Nov 94]

